        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Ahead of the release of her 13th solo album, the fantastically titled Chakzilla, we rank the best of a sublime catalogue of funk, slow jams and tears-on-the-dancefloor disco</p><p>Chaka Khan had harsh words for the “assholes” at her then record company, Warner Bros, who she felt under-promoted 1992’s The Woman I Am, her first album in four years. Listening to Love You All My Lifetime’s cocktail of funk and contemporary R&amp;B, you wonder if she didn’t have a point. There’s no obvious reason why it wasn’t huge hit.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2026/aug/27/aint-nobody-better-chaka-khan-20-best-songs-ranked\">Continue reading...</a>"
